tamente inferior, lo esperable serían 13,8 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 3,6, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,5 a 5,3. En diciembre se adjudicó el 12 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 13 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 46 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.010 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos maliciosos. Puede deberse a necesidades específicas o a precios de mercado. No implica que se haya sobrepasado el límite ni que se haya actuado incorrectamente.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros áreas. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o con demandas específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 50 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 13.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.5 to 5.3. December accounts for 12% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 13% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,010 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be close to the limit due to market conditions or budget constraints. The statistical pattern alone doesn't indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the reason for the amount. Review the contracts of awardee A to see if they repeat the same type of service or supply. Look at the dates and distribution of contracts to assess if there's a consistent pattern or random occurrence.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["dZbjw9F8DX970UvEyYJSGw%3D%3D","aa0FwHeGZ87gL1BHd3qjQA%3D%3D","vV2GytyiHERSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}